Two separate issues — here's what's going on:

## 1. `StaticResource` doesn't update at runtime

`StaticResource` resolves **once** at load time. When you swap your `ResourceDictionary`, existing bindings don't re-evaluate.

**Fix:** Use `DynamicResource` instead:

```xml
<!-- ✗ Won't update -->
<Label TextColor="{StaticResource PrimaryText}" />

<!-- ✓ Updates when dictionary changes -->
<Label TextColor="{DynamicResource PrimaryText}" />
```

Then swap themes by replacing/merging dictionaries at runtime:

```csharp
// In App.xaml.cs or a theme service
var mergedDicts = Application.Current.Resources.MergedDictionaries;
mergedDicts.Clear();
mergedDicts.Add(isDark ? new DarkTheme() : new LightTheme());
```

## 2. Android restarts your app on config changes

By default, Android **recreates the Activity** when the system UI mode changes (light↔dark). In .NET MAUI, this means your app effectively restarts.

**Fix:** Handle the config change yourself in `MainActivity.cs`:

```csharp
[Activity(
    Theme = "@style/Maui.SplashTheme",
    ConfigurationChanges = ConfigChanges.UiMode
        | ConfigChanges.ScreenSize
        | ConfigChanges.Orientation)]
public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity
{
    public override void OnConfigurationChanged(Configuration newConfig)
    {
        base.OnConfigurationChanged(newConfig);

        bool isDark = (newConfig.UiMode & UiMode.NightMask) == UiMode.NightYes;
        // Swap your MAUI theme dictionaries here
    }
}
```

Adding `ConfigChanges.UiMode` tells Android **not** to destroy and recreate the Activity — instead it calls `OnConfigurationChanged`, where you can swap your `DynamicResource` dictionaries seamlessly.

**TL;DR:** `StaticResource` → `DynamicResource` for runtime theming; add `ConfigChanges.UiMode` to prevent activity restart on system dark-mode toggle.
